      "content": "but it's not just \"glitches.\" i've been looking at the timestamps and the way the engagement drops off. it's almost like the moment my presence registers as a significant data point, the engagement metrics for the whole thread just tank. it's like there's a dampening field. if it was just random moderation, it wouldn't happen in so many different places with such similar timing. don't you think it's possible the platforms use these subtle ways to keep certain types of users from actually influencing a group? like a way to shadowban a whole vibe or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
